{\pard \qc \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs36 Footers and Section Breaks Guide\par}
{\pard \qc \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0  Prof.\u160 ?Jack Reilly\par}
{\pard \qc \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0  F2026\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 This guide covers editing footers, aligning page numbers, and deleting section breaks.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Editing the footer and aligning page numbers\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The footer in the report shell will look like this:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\pict\pngblip\picw1084\pich536\picwgoal10915\pichgoal5397 }\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Double click in the footer area, and then you should be able to edit the project title. Change \u8220"Title of Project\u8221" to the actual title of your project.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\pict\pngblip\picw1298\pich604\picwgoal13070\pichgoal6082 }\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Drag the page number box to align with the end of the footer.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\pict\pngblip\picw1072\pich370\picwgoal10794\pichgoal3725 }\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 All done!\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\pict\pngblip\picw1135\pich543\picwgoal7463\pichgoal3570 }\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Deleting section breaks\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Click on the paragraph button (find it on the Home menu, see the image below) to show formatting marks on your report.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\pict\pngblip\picw702\pich170\picwgoal7069\pichgoal1711 }\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Once you click this you will see formatting marks appear in blue, and text in black that shows section breaks and page breaks. Find the section break you want to delete.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\pict\pngblip\picw1102\pich348\picwgoal11097\pichgoal3504 }\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Click and press Command on your keyboard to select the section break. This will highlight it.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\pict\pngblip\picw1094\pich300\picwgoal11016\pichgoal3020 }\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Press Command + X. This will cut the section break out of the report.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\pict\pngblip\picw1072\pich383\picwgoal7048\pichgoal2518 }\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 It should be gone. If not, try a few times \u8211- it can be finicky!\par}
}
